reates an immediate winning threat (Open Four). While Black has a winning move on the board right now, I11 is the maximal play for White, creating the strongest possible shape and forcing a win if the opponent fails to execute their own winning move immediately.\n\nEvaluation: Black has an unstoppable winning position (Open 4 at K8-H11). White\'s best move is to create a counter Open 4 to maximize threats.\nReason: The move I11 extends the diagonal F8-G9-H10 to form an Open 4 (F8-G9-H10-I11). This threatens an unavoidable win for White on the next turn. Although Black can win immediately, this is the strongest move available to White.\nAnswer: { "col": "I", "row": 11 }'}
